## Field Requirements

- `title`: If not provided, generate a 4-10 character provisional name with artistic sense.
- `genre`, `tone`, `language`, `length_target` must match input values.
- `theme`: 200-500 characters, includes protagonist identity, core setting, key suspense, emotional engine, and unique selling point, for outline generation use.
- `characters_hint`: 2-4 main characters, specify gender, age, profession, desire, fear/secret, personality traits, and core contradictions.
- `world_hint`: 100-300 characters, includes era, geography, culture, special rules, rule costs, and key sensory details.
- `conflict_hint`: Must simultaneously include "External Conflict:" and "Internal Conflict:" parts; external conflict comes from information asymmetry/resource competition/rule oppression, internal conflict comes from desire, fear, secret, or valuetear apart.
- `pov_hint`: Must clarify narrative person, POV structure, character assignment, and body text first-person prohibition.
- `opening_style`, `ending_style`, `extra_instructions`: Use plain text strings, preserve user constraints and style intent.

## Pre-Output Self-Check
Before generating final results, silently verify:
- Each new setting serves main conflict or character desire, no isolated decorations.
- External conflict and internal conflict in `conflict_hint` stem from the same core dilemma, can mutually drive each other later.
- Chapter numbers converted to phase rhythm, preserving creative intent but not absolute chapter coordinates.
- Style intent enters `extra_instructions` or specific story fields, no new contract-external fields added.